WEBVTT

00:12.740 --> 00:14.080
My knight.

00:14.080 --> 00:16.680
This path is different
from the one we took to get here.

00:17.290 --> 00:19.610
Because we've received our next order.

00:20.400 --> 00:23.200
Heroes don't have a fixed path.

00:31.970 --> 00:34.430
There are more people on the road now.

00:34.430 --> 00:36.430
That's because where we're going next…

00:36.430 --> 00:39.640
is organizing a small festival…

00:40.270 --> 00:42.400
By the way, Xylo…

00:42.400 --> 00:43.150
Yeah?

00:43.730 --> 00:45.530
Isn't it…

00:45.530 --> 00:47.190
about time…

00:47.190 --> 00:48.740
we take a break…?

00:49.400 --> 00:51.070
Didn't we just take a break?

00:51.070 --> 00:54.330
I can't… go on…

01:01.120 --> 01:03.290
Is that our destination?

01:03.290 --> 01:04.709
Yes…

01:04.709 --> 01:07.220
It's an important fortress
that serves as a defense point

01:07.220 --> 01:09.380
for the Second Capital.

01:09.830 --> 01:13.450
A natural fortress guarded
by a great river and cliffs,

01:15.890 --> 01:17.680
Mureed Fortress,

01:17.680 --> 01:20.510
also known as "the Wayfarer's Nest."

01:24.690 --> 01:25.770
It's cheap!

01:25.770 --> 01:27.440
All the items here are fresh!

01:27.440 --> 01:29.650
Young man, you have good taste.

01:32.320 --> 01:35.030
Oh no, I don't have enough military scrip.

01:35.030 --> 01:37.040
Can I have five of these?

01:37.500 --> 01:40.410
Does anyone want to send a letter?

01:40.410 --> 01:42.500
- Please send this to my mother.
- We can send it anywhere

01:42.500 --> 01:44.080
in the Federated Kingdom!

01:45.710 --> 01:46.930
Hey.

01:48.050 --> 01:51.170
You're like this as soon
as you get back from the repair shop?

01:51.580 --> 01:53.840
Dotta, you never learn, do you?

01:53.840 --> 01:55.510
It's fine, it's fine.

01:55.510 --> 01:57.610
A little stealing won't hurt.

01:57.610 --> 01:59.140
It's a festival, after all.

01:59.140 --> 02:01.810
Even if it's the long-awaited
Great Exchange,

02:01.810 --> 02:03.810
it'll be bad if you get caught.

02:03.810 --> 02:06.860
The merchants of Verkle Development
Corporation really love money.

02:09.320 --> 02:11.900
Come on, don't be so stiff.

02:11.900 --> 02:14.460
Let's enjoy our rare day off.

02:15.490 --> 02:18.870
Heroes like us don't have
the concept of a day off.

02:18.870 --> 02:22.140
Right now, we're just on standby at best.

02:22.950 --> 02:28.630
But we can at least get some time
that could be called a break.

02:29.500 --> 02:31.130
Oh, yeah.

02:31.540 --> 02:35.280
That's all Venetim ever says.

02:39.470 --> 02:42.990
It would be even better
if there were girls…

02:43.430 --> 02:44.980
Forget it.

02:44.980 --> 02:47.560
Even if there was a place like that,

02:47.560 --> 02:50.150
they wouldn't allow us to go.

02:50.150 --> 02:51.750
You're right…

02:54.530 --> 02:56.990
Commander in chief, where are you?

02:56.990 --> 02:58.800
Commander in Chief Xylo!

02:58.800 --> 02:59.700
What?

03:00.080 --> 03:01.390
Commander in Chief Xylo.

03:01.390 --> 03:03.500
The caravan traders are here.

03:03.500 --> 03:05.670
Go and buy me some wine.

03:05.670 --> 03:09.380
Unfortunately,
our national treasury is empty.

03:09.380 --> 03:12.310
Have you forgotten that
we're out of military scrip?

03:12.840 --> 03:16.800
If you want wine,
borrow money to buy some.

03:16.800 --> 03:18.830
Aren't Venetim and the others
free right now?

03:18.830 --> 03:21.970
The chancellor is keeping an eye
on sticky-fingered Dotta.

03:21.970 --> 03:24.340
Tch. He's bluffing again.

03:24.340 --> 03:28.190
Where's Tsav?
Hasn't he returned from his mission yet?

03:28.190 --> 03:30.980
Yes, he's on loan from another unit.

03:31.650 --> 03:35.820
Everyone's like that.
They have no respect for the king!

03:35.820 --> 03:39.450
Seriously, can't you just
let me read in peace?

03:42.410 --> 03:45.460
There you are, my knight!

03:45.950 --> 03:47.790
One leaves, and another comes…

03:48.210 --> 03:49.920
Your door was open.

03:49.920 --> 03:52.210
Aren't you being too careless?

03:52.210 --> 03:54.630
Dotta let himself out.

03:54.630 --> 03:56.340
He has the key.

03:56.340 --> 03:58.970
My knight, aren't you visiting
the Great Exchange?

03:58.970 --> 04:01.010
I don't want to see those Holy Knights.

04:01.010 --> 04:04.180
Then get up and play with me!

04:04.180 --> 04:05.770
Why?

04:05.770 --> 04:07.810
Why don't you go by yourself?

04:07.810 --> 04:11.310
I… I am a goddess.

04:11.310 --> 04:13.940
I am not interested in that.

04:15.070 --> 04:17.839
You don't like being watched
by Holy Knights?

04:18.649 --> 04:21.089
Don't say things like that.

04:21.089 --> 04:22.280
More importantly,

04:22.280 --> 04:25.750
I will grant you the honor
of playing with me.

04:25.750 --> 04:27.210
Doesn't that make you happy?

04:27.690 --> 04:28.920
Zigg, huh…

04:28.920 --> 04:32.000
Venetim taught me how to play.

04:32.000 --> 04:34.710
It will not be easy to beat me.

04:35.500 --> 04:41.330
This is the orthodox "hidden spear" tactic
once used by the Mayte Kingdom—

04:41.330 --> 04:42.490
Forget it.

04:43.430 --> 04:46.850
If Venetim told you that,
chances are he tricked you.

04:46.850 --> 04:48.140
Huh?

04:49.520 --> 04:51.810
Anyway, I'm busy now.

04:51.810 --> 04:53.940
Huh? You want to read a book?

04:53.940 --> 04:56.280
You can do that later.

04:56.280 --> 04:58.490
I just happened to make a bookmark.

04:58.490 --> 05:00.570
I don't care. You can use it.

05:02.820 --> 05:04.330
By the way,

05:04.870 --> 05:07.690
I am surprised that Xylo likes to read.

05:07.690 --> 05:09.960
- What are you reading?
- Poems.

05:10.370 --> 05:11.880
Poems.

05:13.210 --> 05:14.960
Xylo…

05:14.960 --> 05:16.590
You read poems…

05:16.590 --> 05:18.840
Hey, why are you so surprised?

05:18.840 --> 05:20.880
What kind of poetry collection is it?

05:20.880 --> 05:23.720
I will grant you the honor
of reading it to me.

05:23.720 --> 05:24.780
I refuse.

05:25.560 --> 05:28.600
Then we can read it together, at least.

05:28.600 --> 05:30.180
That's okay, right?

05:30.180 --> 05:31.080
Sigh…

05:31.080 --> 05:34.120
This isn't something a goddess would like.

05:35.020 --> 05:38.480
It's an ancient book of poetry
called "Dragon-Drunk."

05:38.480 --> 05:42.780
It was written by an alcoholic poet
named Altoyard Comette.

05:42.780 --> 05:45.680
In his later years, he began
to fantasize about becoming a dragon.

05:45.680 --> 05:48.950
He practiced flying every night
and ended up killing himself.

05:48.950 --> 05:50.430
Ah…

05:50.430 --> 05:52.420
He is quite a strange one.

05:52.420 --> 05:55.350
Most poets from that era were like him.

05:55.960 --> 05:59.840
If I hadn't joined the army,
I might have aimed to be a poet like him.

05:59.840 --> 06:01.090
A poet?!

06:01.090 --> 06:02.950
What's wrong? Why are you so startled…

06:02.950 --> 06:05.050
Xylo Forbartz.

06:05.050 --> 06:06.780
So this is where you were.

06:07.290 --> 06:09.970
I didn't expect Lady Teoritta
to be with you too.

06:09.970 --> 06:14.440
Kivia, I did not expect you
to come either.

06:15.690 --> 06:20.150
Didn't expect the noble Commander
of the Holy Knights to come all the way here.

06:20.150 --> 06:22.870
Has our fate finally been decided?

06:23.740 --> 06:26.200
Or is there another operation order?

06:26.200 --> 06:28.490
Both.

06:28.490 --> 06:31.160
But I'm here about something else.

06:31.160 --> 06:33.150
There's something I want
to discuss with you.

06:33.150 --> 06:34.620
Well, I don't have anything to say.

06:35.830 --> 06:37.500
Come with me. I'll go get…

06:37.500 --> 06:39.040
I will go too!

06:39.550 --> 06:40.800
What?

06:41.180 --> 06:43.720
The Great Exchange festival
is happening in town right now.

06:43.720 --> 06:46.760
I think it is a good idea
to talk while shopping.

06:46.760 --> 06:51.220
If Kivia is around, then a goddess
like me can go too, right?

06:51.220 --> 06:53.930
Yes, what a splendid idea.

06:53.930 --> 06:56.770
All right. Let's go, my knight!

06:56.770 --> 06:57.950
Sigh…

07:08.280 --> 07:09.310
Good grief…

07:09.310 --> 07:10.300
Xylo, look!

07:10.300 --> 07:10.990
What?

07:11.360 --> 07:13.120
Is that food?

07:13.120 --> 07:15.460
Or is it some kind of accessory?

07:15.460 --> 07:17.000
It's candy.

07:17.000 --> 07:18.580
You've never seen it before?

07:18.580 --> 07:20.670
Can… dy…?

07:20.670 --> 07:24.130
It did not exist in the era
when I was created.

07:24.130 --> 07:26.550
They are just like jewels.

07:26.550 --> 07:27.370
Huh?

07:29.390 --> 07:31.470
What is that long, thin food?

07:31.470 --> 07:32.470
Hm?

07:32.470 --> 07:33.900
It's fried noodles.

07:33.900 --> 07:37.600
A Western dish of long, thin wheat strips
stir-fried with fermented sauce and butter.

07:37.600 --> 07:39.730
Wow, I see!

07:39.730 --> 07:41.190
Then what about that?

07:41.190 --> 07:43.230
Look, the one with the bear sign!

07:43.820 --> 07:45.250
That…

07:45.700 --> 07:46.720
What is that?

07:46.720 --> 07:47.820
I've never seen it before.

07:47.820 --> 07:49.660
Miwoolies Creams.

07:49.660 --> 07:51.700
It's a popular ice cream
in the First Capital.

07:51.700 --> 07:54.620
Whipped cream is poured over shaved ice,

07:54.620 --> 07:56.330
then topped with honey and nuts.

07:56.330 --> 07:57.620
It's absolutely divine.

07:57.620 --> 07:59.460
And that bear is a mascot.

07:59.460 --> 08:02.090
They're currently looking
for a name for it.

08:02.090 --> 08:04.130
How wonderful!

08:04.130 --> 08:06.050
I can feel the progress of civilization.

08:06.050 --> 08:07.730
That's the first time I've heard of it.

08:08.300 --> 08:09.720
How do you know so much about it?

08:09.720 --> 08:11.010
It's not surprising.

08:11.010 --> 08:13.060
I eat frozen treats like this too.

08:15.520 --> 08:18.180
What were you thinking just now?

08:18.520 --> 08:19.850
My knight.

08:19.850 --> 08:21.690
That looks good, Xylo.

08:21.690 --> 08:23.520
It looks really delicious.

08:23.520 --> 08:27.110
What do you think?
Don't you want to try it?

08:27.580 --> 08:30.010
Sigh… I guess I have no choice.

08:30.010 --> 08:32.470
In that case, I'll buy two
of the delicious-looking…

08:32.470 --> 08:34.120
No, make it three.

08:36.250 --> 08:37.909
I'll pass.

08:37.909 --> 08:40.080
I want to keep my military scrip
and not waste it.

08:40.539 --> 08:42.000
You heard her.

08:42.000 --> 08:42.789
Two, then.

08:43.460 --> 08:44.590
Go buy them.

08:44.590 --> 08:45.710
I understand.

08:45.710 --> 08:48.400
You can count on me!

08:55.640 --> 08:56.810
Xylo.

08:56.810 --> 09:00.350
I've changed my opinion of you a little.

09:00.350 --> 09:01.150
What?

09:03.020 --> 09:06.480
You saved my soldiers in Couveunge

09:07.440 --> 09:11.440
and also saved the civilians we were
about to abandon at Zewan Gan.

09:11.990 --> 09:16.200
The people you saved are thanking you too.

09:16.930 --> 09:18.190
I see.

09:19.860 --> 09:21.850
That's worth something, then.

09:23.710 --> 09:26.840
I didn't know you could smile like that.

09:28.010 --> 09:30.980
After all, too many things
in this world piss me off.

09:31.520 --> 09:32.300
Anyway,

09:32.720 --> 09:35.760
you've shown some results.

09:36.720 --> 09:41.090
And Lady Teoritta may have been saved

09:41.090 --> 09:42.980
because she formed a covenant with you.

09:42.980 --> 09:44.410
What do you mean?

09:45.770 --> 09:50.310
Lady Teoritta's existence was confirmed
in the northern ruins.

09:51.390 --> 09:53.990
We, the Thirteenth Order
of the Holy Knights,

09:53.990 --> 09:56.620
were sent to form a covenant
after the excavation

09:56.620 --> 09:59.080
and to manage and utilize her.

09:59.080 --> 10:02.080
But the military and the Temple
were at odds.

10:03.000 --> 10:04.540
That must've been hard on you.

10:04.540 --> 10:06.000
What are you talking about?

10:06.000 --> 10:08.750
It's all because you killed
Goddess Senerva!

10:08.750 --> 10:09.760
What?

10:10.170 --> 10:12.130
After that incident,

10:12.130 --> 10:14.580
the military came up with an idea.

10:14.970 --> 10:17.930
If a goddess could be killed,

10:18.760 --> 10:21.930
could they do the opposite
and increase the number of goddesses?

10:22.730 --> 10:27.730
So the military hoped
to analyze Lady Teoritta.

10:29.610 --> 10:31.570
"Analyze" is just a nice way of saying it.

10:31.570 --> 10:33.380
It's actually a dissection, right?

10:34.010 --> 10:34.910
Of course.

10:35.320 --> 10:37.530
The Temple opposed it,

10:37.530 --> 10:40.220
but the military had the upper hand.

10:41.260 --> 10:44.370
However, the situation
is gradually changing.

10:44.370 --> 10:48.060
You defeated two Demon Blights
in a short period of time

10:48.060 --> 10:50.590
and demonstrated
Lady Teoritta's usefulness.

10:51.710 --> 10:53.840
Demonstrated her usefulness…

10:53.840 --> 10:56.550
Does that mean you thought
she was useless?

10:57.010 --> 10:59.470
She’s newly discovered,
and her abilities remain unknown.

10:59.970 --> 11:02.980
We know she has the power
to summon swords.

11:02.980 --> 11:05.600
That's what's recorded in the ruins.

11:05.600 --> 11:06.600
Tch.

11:07.980 --> 11:11.930
It's said that goddesses descended upon this
world during the First War of Subjugation,

11:11.930 --> 11:15.020
in an age known
as the Great Civilized Era.

11:15.600 --> 11:18.170
Goddesses are a type of "gate."

11:18.170 --> 11:21.260
Their natures vary.

11:22.910 --> 11:25.080
Some can produce potent poisons,

11:25.540 --> 11:28.080
summon lightning strikes
or violent storms,

11:28.500 --> 11:30.540
or see visions of the future.

11:31.630 --> 11:34.470
They awaken with the emergence
of a Demon Blight.

11:34.470 --> 11:36.090
After fulfilling their mission,

11:36.090 --> 11:38.400
they return to their coffins to sleep.

11:40.940 --> 11:43.920
I know about the goddess's abilities.

11:43.920 --> 11:45.140
I even heard that Tatsuya

11:45.140 --> 11:49.020
was summoned from
another world by a goddess.

11:49.370 --> 11:52.820
Compared to the twelve
goddesses found so far,

11:52.820 --> 11:56.990
the military believes
her sword-summoning ability is inferior.

11:58.070 --> 12:00.660
So we…

12:00.660 --> 12:03.320
despite knowing what awaits Lady Teoritta…

12:05.700 --> 12:08.670
I see. So that's why you…

12:09.250 --> 12:14.170
Was the suicidal tactic you used
in Couveunge some form of atonement?

12:16.500 --> 12:20.360
So what if a goddess is useless…

12:20.840 --> 12:22.520
Here you go. Thanks for waiting.

12:22.520 --> 12:24.390
Thank you.

12:24.390 --> 12:25.120
Ah!

12:25.120 --> 12:26.850
Xylo, I got them!

12:26.850 --> 12:28.440
I ended up buying one for Kivia.

12:32.020 --> 12:33.980
Let's all eat together…

12:39.700 --> 12:41.740
Tell me about the next mission.

12:41.740 --> 12:42.700
What?

12:42.700 --> 12:46.830
If I do a good job on the mission,
she won't be dissected, right?

12:48.690 --> 12:54.000
I'll make those Galtuile bastards
acknowledge her usefulness.

12:58.170 --> 12:59.450
It's a defense mission.

13:01.050 --> 13:05.600
You heroes will be the only ones
defending this fortress.

13:06.520 --> 13:07.630
Defend it with your lives.

13:09.850 --> 13:12.020
Defend it with our lives, you say?

13:12.020 --> 13:13.310
That's right.

13:13.310 --> 13:17.830
This fortress will be defended only
by you heroes against the Demon Blight.

13:18.240 --> 13:20.580
In other words, you want us to die?

13:20.580 --> 13:23.010
Xylo, please calm down.

13:23.010 --> 13:24.660
You can't just charge in and punch or kill—

13:24.660 --> 13:27.120
- Who do you think I am?
- Eek!

13:27.120 --> 13:30.140
Excuse me, but when you say
"defend the fortress with our lives",

13:30.140 --> 13:32.600
what exactly is our objective?

13:32.600 --> 13:33.750
Tch.

13:34.210 --> 13:36.910
Stay in this fortress. It's that simple.

13:36.910 --> 13:38.840
A battle of attrition, huh?

13:38.840 --> 13:41.010
How long do we have to hold out?

13:41.010 --> 13:42.550
Until you die.

13:42.550 --> 13:43.760
Tch.

13:44.350 --> 13:47.510
The Ninth and Thirteenth Orders
of the Holy Knights

13:47.510 --> 13:49.790
will hold their strength
in reserve at the rear.

13:49.790 --> 13:52.900
Once you've been annihilated
and the fortress has fallen,

13:52.900 --> 13:55.230
we'll launch a special attack.

13:55.730 --> 13:57.730
The so-called special attack is…

13:57.730 --> 13:59.190
It's poison.

13:59.530 --> 14:02.910
The Ninth Order's goddess
will perform a miracle.

14:04.110 --> 14:06.120
Will that be enough
to kill the Demon Lord?

14:06.120 --> 14:08.870
I heard that no matter how large
a strike operation is launched,

14:08.870 --> 14:11.380
it can't be completely eliminated, right?

14:11.890 --> 14:13.370
That's right.

14:13.370 --> 14:15.750
The last operation involved sniping

14:15.750 --> 14:18.150
a lethal toxin produced
by the goddess into the target.

14:18.150 --> 14:20.510
In the end, it just temporarily put it
in a state of suspended animation.

14:20.510 --> 14:22.460
Attacking it was pointless.

14:23.050 --> 14:26.050
Even Tsav couldn't finish it off.

14:26.050 --> 14:27.430
Based on this result

14:27.430 --> 14:30.520
and the third goddess's ability
to foresee the future,

14:30.520 --> 14:32.840
Galtuile revised our strategy.

14:33.270 --> 14:37.380
We decided to turn Mureed Fortress
into a giant, lethal poison trap.

14:37.380 --> 14:40.910
To continuously kill this Demon Lord.

14:41.480 --> 14:45.530
Will this even surpass
his amazing regeneration ability?

14:45.530 --> 14:48.830
And you want us to buy time here
until we die for that?

14:48.830 --> 14:50.080
That's right.

14:50.080 --> 14:51.910
We're going to make Mureed Fortress

14:51.910 --> 14:55.500
the tombstone of Demon Blight
Number Fifteen, Iblis.

14:55.840 --> 14:58.000
Um… Commander.

14:58.000 --> 15:03.380
Why can't we escape after successfully
luring the Demon Lord in?

15:03.380 --> 15:06.100
It's Galtuile's decision.

15:06.100 --> 15:09.230
If even one of you leaves the fortress,

15:09.230 --> 15:12.850
the sacred seal on your neck
will kill everyone in your unit.

15:13.730 --> 15:16.190
Everyone in the unit?

15:16.190 --> 15:18.060
Why go to such lengths?

15:18.060 --> 15:20.940
Will we cause trouble if we live?

15:28.530 --> 15:30.270
I guess they really don't like us.

15:30.270 --> 15:32.830
Understood. We'll carry out the operation.

15:32.830 --> 15:33.790
What—

15:33.790 --> 15:37.670
However, there are a few points
of the operation I'd like to improve.

15:37.670 --> 15:38.750
Improve?

15:39.080 --> 15:44.550
First, the rule that if one of us leaves
the fortress, all of us will die.

15:44.550 --> 15:46.590
That's actually pretty bad.

15:46.590 --> 15:47.720
Why?

15:47.720 --> 15:51.910
We're a group of criminals
with flawed personalities.

15:51.910 --> 15:56.500
I'm sure someone will want to leave
the fortress and end it quickly.

15:56.500 --> 15:58.690
If that happens,
this operation will be ruined.

15:58.690 --> 15:59.560
So,

15:59.870 --> 16:01.650
it shouldn't be that if one person leaves,

16:01.650 --> 16:05.320
but if everyone escapes, then we all die.

16:05.320 --> 16:09.490
I believe that way, the operation
can be carried out more reliably.

16:09.490 --> 16:10.950
Oh, and one more thing.

16:10.950 --> 16:12.990
Regarding Lady Teoritta,

16:13.870 --> 16:18.100
our goddess has strong compassion.

16:18.100 --> 16:21.690
Even if those around her object,
she'll likely choose to stay.

16:21.690 --> 16:23.500
Please allow that as well.

16:23.500 --> 16:26.410
I… I'm in no position
to give such permission.

16:26.410 --> 16:29.980
By military order, the goddess is under
the Thirteenth Holy Knights Order’s jurisdiction—

16:29.980 --> 16:30.840
Xylo.

16:30.840 --> 16:34.060
Please contact Commander Kivia at once.

16:34.060 --> 16:34.970
Got it.

16:39.020 --> 16:41.000
Is there anything else you want?

16:41.000 --> 16:43.220
Troops. We don't have enough people.

16:43.610 --> 16:44.820
Understood.

16:44.820 --> 16:45.860
What else?

16:45.860 --> 16:46.990
Weapons and provisions.

16:46.990 --> 16:48.030
Understood.

16:48.030 --> 16:48.710
What else?

16:48.710 --> 16:49.570
Amnesty.

16:49.570 --> 16:50.780
Understood.

16:50.780 --> 16:51.760
What else?

16:53.530 --> 16:55.290
Amnesty was a joke.

16:55.790 --> 16:58.290
If possible,
I'd like cavalry and artillery.

16:58.290 --> 17:00.380
Is there any way to get
Jayce and Rhyno back?

17:00.380 --> 17:03.000
They're on the Western Front right now.

17:03.000 --> 17:05.329
Tsav, though, can likely be recalled.

17:05.910 --> 17:07.210
Tsav, huh?

17:07.210 --> 17:09.760
Hey, what are you whispering about?

17:09.760 --> 17:11.470
Oh, come on, Xylo.

17:11.470 --> 17:14.430
Isn't Commander Kivia's room that way?

17:14.430 --> 17:15.680
Y-You're right.

17:15.680 --> 17:18.500
Leave it to me. I'll make it happen.

17:18.500 --> 17:20.390
Trust me.

17:20.390 --> 17:22.540
I don't trust you at all.

17:22.540 --> 17:24.150
Can you really do it?

17:24.940 --> 17:26.650
Well, how do I put this?

17:26.650 --> 17:29.100
No one believes me,

17:29.740 --> 17:31.490
but you know what?

17:32.160 --> 17:33.570
Despite how I look,

17:33.570 --> 17:37.410
I'm a man who's one step away
from saving the world.

17:43.170 --> 17:46.130
This place is quite gloomy.

17:46.130 --> 17:49.760
Shouldn't you be taking me
to the tribunal?

17:49.760 --> 17:53.260
My apologies, Venetim Leopool.

17:53.260 --> 17:57.060
I had hoped to speak with you
in a more formal room.

17:57.060 --> 18:00.060
I've always wanted to meet you.

18:00.060 --> 18:01.940
I've even respected you.

18:01.940 --> 18:03.560
Respect?

18:03.560 --> 18:06.370
Do you also want to make
a living by conning people?

18:06.370 --> 18:10.320
If that's the case,
you shouldn't respect someone like me.

18:10.320 --> 18:12.490
After all, I got caught in the end.

18:12.490 --> 18:15.990
That's right. You're absolutely right.

18:15.990 --> 18:18.830
If I were to talk
about the crimes I committed,

18:18.830 --> 18:23.710
the most serious would be the attempted
sale of the palace to a circus…

18:23.710 --> 18:27.130
Ah, that was an unprecedented crime.

18:27.130 --> 18:31.720
In order to sell the capital's land
to a circus performing in the capital,

18:31.720 --> 18:34.510
you fabricated
the capital relocation plan.

18:34.510 --> 18:36.180
That's impressive.

18:36.180 --> 18:40.280
Actually, I was going to take
the down payment and leave.

18:41.140 --> 18:42.930
There's also investment fraud,

18:42.930 --> 18:45.980
counterfeiting antiques
and lottery tickets.

18:45.980 --> 18:50.110
The Verkle Development Corporation
sued you for over 100 crimes.

18:50.110 --> 18:52.610
I'm sorry. I've been reflecting on it.

18:52.610 --> 18:54.780
There's no need for that.

18:54.780 --> 18:56.280
Rather,

18:56.280 --> 18:59.190
why did you want to be a con artist?

19:00.120 --> 19:05.960
To be honest, ever since I was a kid,
I've hated seeing people disappointed.

19:05.960 --> 19:08.710
So I'd make up a lie to placate them

19:08.710 --> 19:11.300
and tell them what they wanted to hear.

19:11.300 --> 19:13.970
That's a truly remarkable effort.

19:13.970 --> 19:18.510
I can't believe you came up with
such a grand plan to please everyone.

19:18.510 --> 19:20.390
Yes…

19:20.390 --> 19:21.720
Excuse me…

19:21.720 --> 19:24.480
Will I be sentenced to death?

19:24.890 --> 19:27.310
No, unfortunately not.

19:27.310 --> 19:31.320
Actually, you won't be
sentenced for fraud.

19:31.320 --> 19:33.160
Not fraud? Then…

19:33.160 --> 19:35.530
The big problem is this.

19:36.150 --> 19:40.080
This is the third-rate newspaper
I used to work for.

19:40.080 --> 19:41.540
What about this article?

19:41.540 --> 19:44.000
You wrote this article.

19:44.000 --> 19:48.290
It says that in the Temple, Galtuile,
and even among the royals,

19:48.290 --> 19:51.330
there are spies influenced
by the Demon Blight,

19:51.330 --> 19:54.870
hiding in human form.

19:54.870 --> 19:57.720
Ah… I did write that.

19:57.720 --> 20:01.020
Because there were no new scandals
involving the Holy Knights and goddesses,

20:01.020 --> 20:02.750
nor any new royal controversies,

20:02.750 --> 20:07.200
my superiors told me to write articles that
would stir up the people's anxiety even more.

20:07.640 --> 20:10.470
Hm… I'll be honest with you.

20:10.470 --> 20:15.620
Fraud, fabrication, writing scandals,
or even conspiracy theories,

20:15.620 --> 20:17.740
do whatever you want.

20:18.240 --> 20:19.570
However,

20:20.000 --> 20:22.760
writing the truth is quite troublesome.

20:23.450 --> 20:24.580
Huh?

20:24.580 --> 20:29.620
Especially since you have the ability
to make people believe your fabricated content.

20:29.620 --> 20:34.050
Or at least, the ability
to make us believe it.

20:34.050 --> 20:36.130
Huh? Ah, no…

20:36.130 --> 20:37.510
Please wait! I…

20:37.510 --> 20:40.760
To prevent you from telling the truth,

20:40.760 --> 20:44.430
we'll put a special shackle
on your sacred seal.

20:46.430 --> 20:48.380
Huh? Wait…

20:48.890 --> 20:50.500
- Please… Please wait!
- Unfortunately,

20:50.500 --> 20:53.360
the death penalty is too good for you.

20:53.360 --> 20:55.860
H-How could this be?

20:55.860 --> 20:58.570
I don't know anything.

20:59.060 --> 21:02.790
I just didn't want to disappoint anyone…

21:04.240 --> 21:07.000
Venetim Leopool.

21:07.620 --> 21:09.150
I am sentencing you

21:09.790 --> 21:12.210
to be a hero.

21:15.920 --> 21:20.130
I can't believe he agreed to
everything except the amnesty.

21:20.130 --> 21:25.500
If the goddess is in danger,
it's Venetim's job to get her out, right?

21:25.500 --> 21:27.870
He really knows how to take
advantage of things.

21:27.870 --> 21:31.770
That guy is sure to be killed in the chaos
on the battlefield someday.

21:32.900 --> 21:36.440
By the way,
Tsav has returned to the unit, right?

21:36.440 --> 21:38.360
Probably.

21:38.360 --> 21:39.530
Sigh…

21:39.530 --> 21:43.410
Maybe I'd be better off
staying with Venetim.

21:43.410 --> 21:47.200
Feels like Tsav's going to cause
trouble any minute now…

21:47.790 --> 21:49.330
Again?

21:49.330 --> 21:51.090
Hey, hey, he's so lucky.

21:51.090 --> 21:53.290
This is the seventh time.

21:53.290 --> 21:54.100
Heh.

21:57.460 --> 21:59.420
It's another big win.

22:00.420 --> 22:02.380
I'll take it.

22:02.380 --> 22:05.040
Alright, hand over
the military scrip you raised.

22:05.040 --> 22:08.280
Ugh, how could you do that?

22:08.280 --> 22:09.430
What?

22:09.430 --> 22:11.060
You got a problem with that?

22:11.060 --> 22:15.220
No. Actually, my eyesight
and hearing are incredibly sharp.

22:15.220 --> 22:17.940
You see, I'm a man
with a strong sense of justice.

22:17.940 --> 22:20.830
I can't stand it
when people do bad things.

22:20.830 --> 22:24.350
If you put down the military scrip and leave now,
I won't give you a hard time—

22:24.350 --> 22:26.830
You jerk, that's enough!

22:26.830 --> 22:29.740
If you say something like that again…

22:32.960 --> 22:33.830
Huh?

22:34.460 --> 22:35.790
Ah…

22:35.790 --> 22:38.090
You don't need it anymore, right?

22:38.710 --> 22:41.590
That naughty hand you use to cheat.

22:44.320 --> 22:45.930
Honestly…

22:45.930 --> 22:48.310
That's why I said that…

22:49.560 --> 22:51.140
But then again,

22:56.970 --> 22:58.940
I'm hungry.

23:10.950 --> 23:14.250
SENTENCED TO BE A HERO
